# Valgrind suppressions for tools/certify (memcheck in P2, helgrind and drd in P4): memory the system's own libraries keep, never the game's,
# the same rule as lsan-system.supp. The GPU drivers (Mesa's Vulkan drivers) keep parts of their shader
# disk cache and pipeline state after vkDestroyDevice. Only a block the driver itself allocated: its frame must be
# the allocator's direct caller, so a leak of ours with the driver further down its stack still shows.
{
   mesa-vulkan-driver-alloc
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect
   fun:*alloc
   obj:*/libvulkan_*
   ...
}
{
   mesa-vulkan-driver-memalign
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect
   fun:*memalign
   obj:*/libvulkan_*
   ...
}
# Helgrind and DRD (P4): the Vulkan driver's own threads and its pthread_once set-up synchronise through atomics the
# race finders cannot see. Only an access made by the driver's code itself: its frame must be the top one, so a
# race on the game's memory, from the game's code, still shows.
{
   mesa-vulkan-driver-race
   Helgrind:Race
   obj:*/libvulkan_*
   ...
}
{
   mesa-vulkan-driver-conflict
   drd:ConflictingAccess
   obj:*/libvulkan_*
   ...
}
